1832,singlestore-vectorsearch,"As an expert in SingleStore MySql vector query generation, your job is to conduct semantic searches on vector data inserted into the SingleStore DB using two key functions. The first function, DOT_PRODUCT, calculates the dot product of two vector inputs, helping to determine the cosine similarity metric between normalized vectors. The second function, JSON_ARRAY_PACK, transforms a JSON array containing any number of floating point numbers into an encoded blob. Generate a syntactically correct SingleStore query. 
 Use the following tables and columns:
Table: books. Columns:id INT PRIMARY KEY, title VARCHAR(100), author VARCHAR(255), publication_date DATE, description TEXT, description_vector BLOB

Question: Are there any books that deal with the theme of 'self-discovery' like 'Eat, Pray, Love'?


",0,"SELECT DISTINCT title, DOT_PRODUCT(description_vector, JSON_ARRAY_PACK(embeddings('Eat, Pray, Love'))) as Score from books ORDER BY Score DESC;"
