  3: r = x * a / (v * 15)
",89,{1}
1870,solve-for-variable,"You are expected to reply to a multiple-choice question. In your response, your final answer as the option number should be enclosed in curly brackets like so: {number}. An option number enclosed in curly brackets should appear only once in your response, as this is the one answer you will be evaluated on.

If
  w = 27 - (-24 / (h - (9 + 36 / m) - x)) / 26 + 21
then which of the following is true?
  1: x = h - (9 + 36 / m) - -24 / ((27 - (w - 21)) * 26)
  2: x = h - (9 + 36 / m) + -24 * ((27 + w + 21) / 26)
  3: x = h - (9 + 36 / m) + -24 * ((27 + w - 21) / 26)
  4: x = h - (9 + 36 / m) - -24 * ((27 + w + 21) / 26)
",94,{1}
1871,solve-for-variable,"You are expected to reply to a multiple-choice question. In your response, your final answer as the option number should be enclosed in curly brackets like so: {number}. An option number enclosed in curly brackets should appear only once in your response, as this is the one answer you will be evaluated on.

If
  s = -((x - m) / 17 + n + 5)
then which of the following is true?
  1: m = x + (s - 5 + n) * 17
  2: m = x + (5 - s + n) * 17
  3: m = x - -(s + 5 + n) * 17
  4: m = x + (s + 5 + n) / 17
",98,{3}
